  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maryland's federal contract obligations are $25.2B for FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 70,373 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $358K. Obligations are down 36.5% year over year, reflecting a smaller fiscal-year-to-date total compared with prior full fiscal years. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Maryland, obligating $10.1B so far. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $4.9B, and the Department of Energy has obligated $1.9B. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the top vendor with $1.4B, and ORANO FEDERAL SERVICES LLC and AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC each have $900M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry category with $2.8B in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $2.7B and Computer Systems Design Services at $2.6B. All figures are contract obligations and represent a fiscal-year-to-date snapshot, not full-year totals.",
